  "description": "Deployment guidance and a configuration marker for running PostQuantum.DataProtection under FIPS 140-3 compliance regimes. This package ships the FipsDeploymentMarker type that hosts can use to declare a FIPS-only operating mode, plus a runtime check that fails fast when the active cryptographic provider does not match the declared posture. The actual FIPS-validated ML-KEM implementation must be supplied by the consumer (e.g. BouncyCastle FIPS or a vendor-validated module). See the README for the full integration guide.",
